  "question": {
    "text": "Let $a_1, a_2, a_3, \\ldots$ be an A.P, such that $\\frac{a_1+a_2+\\ldots+a_p}{a_1+a_2+a_3+\\ldots+a_q}=\\frac{p^3}{q^3} ; p \\neq q$. Then $\\frac{a_6}{a_{21}}$ is equal to:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5uWsd",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{41}{11}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1LGM0",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{31}{121}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "jEmCg",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{11}{41}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LdaqW",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{121}{1861}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{a_1+a_2+a_3+\\ldots \\ldots+a_p}{a_1+a_2+a_3+\\ldots \\ldots+a_q}=\\frac{p^3}{q^3} \\\\ \\Rightarrow & \\frac{a_1+a_2}{a_1}=\\frac{8}{1} \\Rightarrow a_1+\\left(a_1+d\\right)=8 a_1 \\\\ \\Rightarrow \\quad & d=6 a_1 \\\\ & \\text { Now } \\frac{a_6}{a_{21}}=\\frac{a_1+5 d}{a_1+20 d} \\\\ = & \\frac{a_1+5 \\times 6 a_1}{a_1+20 \\times 6 a_1}=\\frac{1+30}{1+120}=\\frac{31}{121}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
